{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787821816571856426,"compiled_state":{"alias":"dire-expectable-terrapin","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"826e55856ae8586c3ac17d92bf873b582d70e2a96db9b884d9ffd36c9a4506aa","event_uuid":"4bf44666-ed4a-4ddd-a4b3-e0eaf32b046d","position":{"commit_sha":"71675dbaa912b6cd4a20d75ccd655fa2139546d8","position":"1787815714183494711-4bf44666-ed4a-4ddd-a4b3-e0eaf32b046d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"efd5dbb3a12a01b4e761d6c9199c0d9cc878038623a829927600f71cef0f91b3","event_uuid":"84ec998c-f0c5-4047-bb40-927219f6a345","position":{"commit_sha":"7efd8846b9584015b995d2fa99fd4c71050f9fcd","position":"1787815745681066998-84ec998c-f0c5-4047-bb40-927219f6a345"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"392fc9a573b4c6449212f59b52bd4a18444b73179d4f882ba21e518224db4158","event_uuid":"9a7c4714-898a-4d70-b4d9-43c74d7e38a7","position":{"commit_sha":"4ae1cf5025c0e7871ef324c8876ec44d75f989f3","position":"1787815752551089415-9a7c4714-898a-4d70-b4d9-43c74d7e38a7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787815714183494711,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"84ec998c-f0c5-4047-bb40-927219f6a345","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1eb6-65f2-5a4e-4c7b"},{"link_uuid":"9a7c4714-898a-4d70-b4d9-43c74d7e38a7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3d86-9fc2-6095-4c69"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe deployed MCP server mints op-cert signatures it can never verify. Every attestation it\nproduces — including the completion-verifier attestation it signs on every close — is\npermanently uncertifiable on the same box.\n\nObserved 2026-08-27 against the LIVE MCP server\n(`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`, container `compose-mcp-1`), signing and then\nimmediately verifying on the same server:\n\n```\nsign_manifest {\"ticket_id\": \"ruby-griffinish-goitered\", \"manifest\": [\"probe: ...\"]}\n  -> {\"algorithm\": \"sshsig\", \"key_id\": \"9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65\",\n      \"signed_at\": 1787815608646086582, \"envelope\": \"{...}\"}          # SUCCEEDS\n\nverify_signature {\"ticket_id\": \"ruby-griffinish-goitered\"}\n  -> {\"verified\": false, \"verdict\": \"foreign_key\", \"step_count\": 1,\n      \"key_id\": \"9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65\", \"head_sha\": \"unknown\",\n      \"reason\": \"this environment has no op-cert public key; it cannot certify any signature\"}\n```\n\nThe signature is not foreign — the principal matches this environment. It is unverifiable\nbecause the matching PUBLIC key is absent.\n\n## Mechanism\n`src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:528-535`\n\n```python\nown_pub = _opcert_own_public_key(tracker)\nif not own_pub:\n    return {\n        **base,\n        \"verified\": False,\n        \"verdict\": \"foreign_key\",\n        \"reason\": \"this environment has no op-cert public key; it cannot certify any signature\",\n    }\n```\n\n`_opcert_own_public_key` reads the public key from the TRACKER directory, but the deployment\nsupplies only the PRIVATE key, via `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY`, from a mount that has no\npublic half. Verified in-container:\n\n```\n$ docker exec compose-mcp-1 ls -l /run/secrets/\n-rw-------. 1 root root 298 Aug 26 18:24 mcp-static-tokens.json\n-rw-------. 1 root root 411 Aug 26 18:24 opcert-ed25519-key          # private key only, no .pub\n\n$ docker exec compose-mcp-1 ls -la /var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets/ | grep -iE 'opcert|env-id|ensure'\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root 152 Aug 27 01:38 .ensure-applied\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root  37 Aug 27 01:09 .env-id                     # no .opcert-key.pub\n```\n\nEnv: `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key`,\n`REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID=9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65`.\n\nThe tracker's `.env-id` is dated 2026-08-27 01:09 and the container started 01:38 — i.e. the\ntracker was re-cloned (see `7be0edb7132d fix(mcp): re-clone an unusable tickets store`). The\nre-clone regenerated `.env-id` but never restored `.opcert-key.pub`. `fsck` on the same server\nnames exactly this failure mode:\n\n```\nENV_ID_MISMATCH: ... This is the signature of a tracker re-clone that did not carry over its\ngit-ignored local state (.env-id, .opcert-key, .opcert-key.pub, .ensure-applied).\n```\n\nso the diagnostic already exists; nothing acts on it, and signing proceeds regardless.\n\n## Impact\nrebar mints exactly two op-cert kinds (ADR 0049): plan-review at claim and\ncompletion-verifier at close. On this server both are signed-but-uncertifiable. Concretely,\nclosing probe bug `weary-paralyzing-xanclomys` returned\n`\"completion_signature\": {\"signed\": true, \"cause\": \"signed\"}` — a certificate that\n`verify_signature` cannot certify. Any project that later enables\n`verify.require_environment` + `verify.opcert_enforce_since` (the enforcement flip in\n`infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`) would find every attestation this server\nproduced rejected as `foreign_key`, and the audit trail silently records certificates that\nprove nothing today.\n\nSigning SUCCEEDS while verification is structurally impossible, so nothing surfaces the\nproblem at the moment the certificate is minted.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Against the deployed MCP server, call `sign_manifest` on any ticket with a one-item manifest.\n2. Observe it succeeds and returns an `sshsig` envelope.\n3. Call `verify_signature` on the same ticket.\n4. Observe `verdict: \"foreign_key\"`, `verified: false`, reason \"this environment has no op-cert public key\".\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1: On the deployed MCP server, a `sign_manifest` immediately followed by `verify_signature` on the same ticket returns `verdict: \"certified\"`, `verified: true`.\n- [ ] AC2: The deployment materializes the public key half wherever `_opcert_own_public_key` reads it, derived from or shipped alongside `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY`.\n- [ ] AC3: A completion attestation signed by a close through the deployed server verifies as `certified` via `verify_signature` with `kind=\"completion-verifier\"`.\n- [ ] AC4: Signing refuses, or emits an explicit warning, when the environment cannot verify its own signatures — a certificate that can never be certified must not be minted silently.\n- [ ] AC5: The tracker re-clone path restores or regenerates the git-ignored local state it destroys (`.opcert-key`, `.opcert-key.pub`, `.env-id`), or fails loudly instead of leaving the environment unable to certify.\n- [ ] AC6: A startup or deploy health check fails when the signing key has no usable public counterpart, so this cannot regress silently.\n\n## Definition of Done\n- [ ] DD1: AC1 and AC3 demonstrated against a deployed MCP server.\n- [ ] DD2: AC4 and AC5 covered by regression tests.\n- [ ] DD3: AC6 check runs in the deploy path.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","1eb6-65f2-5a4e-4c7b"],["relates_to","3d86-9fc2-6095-4c69"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mcp","deploy","opcert","attestation"],"ticket_id":"d26a-8ffa-97cd-4b2a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Deployed MCP server signs op-certs it cannot verify: the signing key has no public counterpart, so every attestation is foreign_key","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4bf44666-ed4a-4ddd-a4b3-e0eaf32b046d","84ec998c-f0c5-4047-bb40-927219f6a345","9a7c4714-898a-4d70-b4d9-43c74d7e38a7"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787821816571856426,"uuid":"20035260-238a-4bfd-9f8b-212f1c6a29b8"}